WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.400
Why do these two matter?

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.319
The compliant network check binds sign-in
and token use to the agency's own path,

3
00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:09.875
so a token stolen and replayed
from somewhere else fails.

4
00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:14.325
In attack terms, it interrupts
credential access and defense evasion.

5
00:00:14.325 --> 00:00:18.387
Universal tenant restrictions
keep agency devices from signing

6
00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:22.450
in to a personal or hostile tenant,
which interrupts exfiltration.

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.375
Both are powerful, and
both can lock people out.

8
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:28.647
So in this module you learn
their failure modes first,

9
00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:32.640
and you run each in report-only or
a pilot before it blocks anyone.
